@slin1237 Could you please reopen this PR for review? It was closed by the idle-PR cleanup, and I would like to prioritize this small startup fix.

With `--skip-server-warmup`, the single `/freeze_gc` POST can run before the HTTP listener is ready, so the GC freeze is missed. Current `main` still has the single-shot call. This PR adds bounded retries for connection failures, with three CPU regression cases covering recovery, retry exhaustion, and immediate handling of HTTP errors. The earlier delayed-listener reproducer failed before the change and succeeded on attempt 5 afterward; the existing regression tests passed.

Could you reopen it so review and CI can continue? I can rebase and rerun the checks for the updated head as needed. Thanks!

